A||||12||Predator||FYI on Pioneer 4X10 TS-A4103 speakers||||7||
Z||000000||Predator||03-29-2001||09:01 AM||||I just wanted to pass along that I bought a pair of Pioneer TS-A4103 4X10 speakers to replace the ones I cracked in the dash, and they work great. If you are looking for a stock looking replacement that you can change out in about 15 minutes I recommend them. They fit perfectly in the dash. I am not going to win a boom boom show, but I like them. They do sound better than the stock ones. They were $96.00 at Circuit City.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||03-29-2001||06:30 PM||||I have a pair of those im my car, I really like the way they sound. With my 160 watt amp on them, they hit so low and hard things start making noises in the dash :P. Now the 4x6's are another story....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||03-29-2001||06:40 PM||||I had a set of those in my 84 coupe. I liked them better than the 4x10 Kickers I have now. I think Kenwood makes a good set of 4x10's too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jake_Dragon||03-29-2001||07:16 PM||||Just replace mine as well. Love the sound.<BR>I had an after market tape player and it made the speakers sound terrible, put in a JVC KD-S570 CD Receiver and it rocks $109.19 at Circuit City. Ya gotta know someone  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/rebel33/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||RossT||03-30-2001||12:22 AM||||online car stereo has them for $79 and free shipping. <A HREF="http://www.onlinecarstereo.com/caraudio/category.asp?c=4&m=3" TARGET=_blank>http://www.onlinecarstereo.com/caraudio/category.asp?c=4&m=3</A> <P>I bought the Kenwoods 4X10 and am very happy.||||reg||1
